From: zhangjianguo <janegle@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] xray-core: allow -l: cgo LDFLAGS under Go 1.27

Go 1.27 (immortalwrt packages feed, 2026-11-11) started rejecting the
`-l:libcronet.a` flag emitted by
github.com/sagernet/cronet-go/lib/linux_arm64_musl:

    invalid flag in #cgo LDFLAGS: -l:libcronet.a
    (see https://go.dev/s/invalidflag)

which breaks xray-core compile with with_naive_outbound. CGO accepts an
explicit allowlist regex via CGO_LDFLAGS_ALLOW; scope it to this package
only. Drop this once cronet-go stops using the -l: form.

--- a/xray-core/Makefile
+++ b/xray-core/Makefile
@@ -19,5 +19,9 @@ PKG_BUILD_PARALLEL:=1
 PKG_USE_MIPS16:=0
 PKG_BUILD_FLAGS:=no-mips16
 
+# Go >=1.27 rejects `-l:libcronet.a` from cronet-go cgo LDFLAGS;
+# allow the -l: form for this package only (go.dev/s/invalidflag).
+export CGO_LDFLAGS_ALLOW:=-l:.*
+
 GO_PKG:=github.com/xtls/xray-core
 GO_PKG_LDFLAGS:=-s -w
